- `test_fit_mil_finds_positive_instance` in [tests/test_probe_fit.py](tests/test_probe_fit.py): It is an existing test updated for the `Fitted.head` return type.

### 2. Does any test depend on implementation details instead of behavior?

Yes. `test_probe_fit_passes_device` in [tests/test_probe_fit_cli.py](tests/test_probe_fit_cli.py) depends on implementation details.

It monkeypatches `fit.fit_condition` and asserts on internal call keyword arguments. It does not verify observable CLI behavior or outputs.

The tests in [tests/test_probe_fit_device.py](tests/test_probe_fit_device.py) test observable outputs and public function contracts, not implementation details.

